    "q-90564": {
      "dom_id": "step-q90564",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=1.9,$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{3}, & 0<x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{8}, & 1\\le x<5, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{5}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot 2{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{5}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{6}}{3}|}_{0}^{1}+{\\frac{{x}^{3}}{24}|}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =5.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =5.5-{(1.9)}^{2} \\\\  & =1.89.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
