    "q-131166": {
      "dom_id": "step-q131166",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{3}{2},$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{4{x}^{3}},\\, & 1<x<3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{9}{4{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{9}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{9}{4}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{4}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{4}-\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
