    "q-131261": {
      "dom_id": "step-q131261",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{7}{8},$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}, & 0<x<1 \\\\ \\frac{3(x-1)}{{x}^{5}},\\, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3(x-1)}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{3x-3}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}|}_{0}^{1}+(-\\frac{3}{x}+\\frac{3}{2{x}^{2}}){|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+3-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}-{(\\frac{7}{8})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{63}{64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
